    "MITRE TTPs": ["T1566.001: Phishing", "T1195.002: Malvertising", "T1071.001: Application Layer Protocol", "T1059.001: PowerShell", "T1055: Process Injection", "T1204.002: User Execution: Malicious File"],
    "Impact": "The exact scale of the campaign is not provided, but Bumblebee is known to deliver Cobalt Strike beacons, information-stealing malware, and various ransomware strains. *Bumblebee also integrates sophisticated evasion techniques and anti-analysis tricks, executing malware entirely in memory through the SelfReg table within MSI files, and has a high threat score of 8.5/10. The malware is capable of performing token manipulation, code injections, and employs anti-VM checks* (https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/new-bumblebee-malware-replaces-contis-bazarloader-in-cyberattacks/; https://cybersecsentinel.com/bumblebee-malware-adapts-to-evade-detection-in-new-attack-campaign/; https://www.infosecurity-magazine.com/news/possible-bumblebee-resurgence/; https://cloudsek.com/blog/technical-analysis-of-bumblebee-malware-loader).",
