 Additional Information: An international law enforcement operation codenamed 'Operation Endgame' seized over 100 malware loader servers and arrested four cybercriminals, with 16 location searches across Europe. *Europol’s ‘Most Wanted’ list now includes eight fugitives linked to these malware operations. One suspect earned at least 69 million Euros in cryptocurrency from renting out infrastructure for ransomware deployment. ReliaQuest uncovered these operations and provided intelligence* (https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/police-seize-over-100-malware-loader-servers-arrest-four-cybercriminals-operation-endgame/; https://securityaffairs.com/170306/malware/security-affairs-malware-newsletter-round-17.html). *The report by Netskope Threat Labs was authored by Leandro Fróes* (https://www.infosecurity-magazine.com/news/possible-bumblebee-resurgence/). *Technical analysis of Bumblebee loader reveals in-line hooks, anti-VM checks, and usage of gdiplus.dll for payload deployment* (https://cloudsek.com/blog/technical-analysis-of-bumblebee-malware-loader). 


