# Enriched Doc (enrihcments marked with *content*(link)): 
 Incident: Fake attachment. Roundcube mail server attacks exploit CVE-2024-37383 vulnerability 

 Root cause: The root cause behind the incident is a stored cross-site scripting (XSS) vulnerability in the Roundcube Webmail email client (CVE-2024-37383). The vulnerability allows attackers to execute JavaScript code on the user's page by exploiting improper validation of SVG tag attributes. *The vulnerability was introduced on June 6, 2024, due to improper sanitization of SVG animate attributes* (https://security.snyk.io/vuln/SNYK-PHP-ROUNDCUBEROUNDCUBEMAIL-8235206). *The CWE classification is CWE-79* (https://vuldb.com/?id.267396). *The exploitability is easy, and a public exploit is available* (https://vuldb.com/?id.267396). 

 Threat Actor/group/campaign: While the blog mentions a previous attack linked to the Winter Vivern group, it states that this specific attack cannot be linked to known actors based on the available information. 

 Organization/industry/location: The victim targeted in this incident is a governmental organization in a CIS (Commonwealth of Independent States) country. 

 Start date – End date: The email was sent in June 2024, and the vulnerability was patched on May 19, 2024. The attack was discovered in September 2024. 

 MITRE TTPs: {'Execution': 'T059.007 - JavaScript', 'Collection': 'T1056.004 - Web portal capture'} 

 Impact: Login credentials and email messages of the affected users were potentially compromised. 

 Mitigation: {'Step 1': 'Update Roundcube Webmail to version 1.5.6 or later, or version 1.6.7 or later, to patch the CVE-2024-37383 vulnerability.', 'Step 2': 'Regularly review and apply security updates for all software components.', 'Step 3': 'Implement email filtering solutions to detect and block malicious emails.', 'Step 4': 'Educate users on identifying phishing emails and suspicious attachments.', 'Step 5': 'Use Web Application Firewalls (WAFs) to filter out malicious web traffic.'} 

 Detection Signature: {'Service': 'Roundcube Webmail', 'Port': '80/443', 'Severity': 'Critical', 'Incident': 'CVE-2024-37383 Exploitation', 'Signature name': '"Roundcube Webmail XSS Vulnerability"', 'Internal checks': {'Ensure Roundcube Webmail is updated to the latest secure version.': '', 'Validate proper sanitization of SVG tags and attributes within email content.': ''}, 'External scanning': {'Monitor for suspicious email patterns attempting to exploit XSS vulnerabilities.': '', 'Detect and block emails containing malicious JavaScript code.': ''}} 

 domain: libcdn.org 

 domain: rcm.codes 

 Additional Info: *Positive Technologies researchers confirmed the phishing emails tricked recipients into revealing sensitive credentials by injecting fake login forms into Roundcube’s interface* (https://socradar.io/roundcube-vulnerability-cve-2024-37383-exploited-in-phishing-attacks-targeting-government-agencies-for-credential-theft/). *Attackers used the ManageSieve plugin to retrieve emails from compromised accounts* (https://socradar.io/roundcube-vulnerability-cve-2024-37383-exploited-in-phishing-attacks-targeting-government-agencies-for-credential-theft/). *Emails contained hidden malicious base64-encoded JavaScript* (https://socradar.io/roundcube-vulnerability-cve-2024-37383-exploited-in-phishing-attacks-targeting-government-agencies-for-credential-theft/). *The CVSS score for the vulnerability is 5.1, and the exploit maturity is classified as Mature* (https://security.snyk.io/vuln/SNYK-PHP-ROUNDCUBEROUNDCUBEMAIL-8235206). *The vulnerability has been added to the CISA Known Exploited Vulnerabilities Catalog* (https://vuldb.com/?id.267396). *The current exploit price range is $0-$5k* (https://vuldb.com/?id.267396). 


