span> </p> </td> </tr> <tr style="height: 53.0078px;"> <td style="border: 1pt solid #cccccc; width: 20.5866%; height: 53.0078px;"> <p style="text-align: center;"> <span style="font-size: 10px;"> SQLTELEMETRY$HL </span> </p> </td> <td style="border: 1pt solid #cccccc; width: 19.3774%; height: 53.0078px;"> <p style="text-align: center;"> <span style="font-size: 10px;"> MSSQL$OPTIMA </span> </p> </td> <td style="border: 1pt solid #cccccc; width: 19.982%; height: 53.0078px;"> <p style="text-align: center;"> <span style="font-size: 10px;"> SQLSERVERAGENT </span> </p> </td> <td style="border: 1pt solid #cccccc; width: 19.982%; height: 53.0078px;"> <p style="text-align: center;"> <span style="font-size: 10px;"> SQLAgent$VEEAMSQL2012 </span> </p> </td> <td style="border: 1pt solid #cccccc; width: 19.982%; height: 53.0078px;"> <p style="text-align: center;"> <span style="font-size: 10px;"> SQLAgent$OPTIMA </span> </p> </td> </tr> <tr style="height: 53.0078px;"> <td style="border: 1pt solid #cccccc; width: 20.5866%; height: 53.0078px;"> <p style="text-align: center;"> <span style="font-size: 10px;"> Veeam </span> </p> </td> <td style="border: 1pt solid #cccccc; width: 19.3774%; height: 53.0078px;"> <p style="text-align: center;"> <span style="font-size: 10px;"> Wuauserv </span> </p> </td> <td style="border: 1pt solid #cccccc; width: 19.982%; height: 53.0078px;"> <p style="text-align: center;"> <span style="font-size: 10px;"> SQLBrowser </span> </p> </td> <td style="border: 1pt solid #cccccc; width: 19.982%; height: 53.0078px;"> <p style="text-align: center;"> <span style="font-size: 10px;"> MSSQL </span> </p> </td> <td style="border: 1pt solid #cccccc; width: 19.982%; height: 53.0078px;"> <p style="text-align: center;"> <span style="font-size: 10px;"> TMBMServer </span> </p> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p> </p> <h3 style="font-weight: normal; font-size: 30px;"> <span style="color: #000000;"> Shadow Copy Delete </span> </h3> <p> When Shadow Copy delete process is initiated by Beast Ransomware, it calls the <strong> IWbemServices::ExecQuery(“WQL”, ”Select * FROM Win32_ShadowCopy”) </strong> WQL query to get the <strong> IEnumWbemClassObject </strong> object for querying shadow copies and <strong> IWbemServices::DeleteInstance(“\\MachineName\ROOT\CIMV2:Win32_ShadowCopy.ID=”{Shadow Copy ID}””) </strong> to delete them. </p> <p> <span style="font-size: 14px;"> <img alt="beast-ransomware-blog-13" height="156" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 878px) 100vw, 878px" src="https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-13.png?width=878&amp;height=156&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-13.png" srcset="https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-13.png?width=439&amp;height=78&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-13.png 439w, https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-13.png?width=878&amp;height=156&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-13.png 878w, https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-13.png?width=1317&amp;height=234&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-13.png 1317w, https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-13.png?width=1756&amp;height=312&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-13.png 1756w, https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-13.png?width=2195&amp;height=390&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-13.png 2195w, https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-13.png?width=2634&amp;height=468&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-13.png 2634w" style="height: auto; max-width: 100%; width: 878px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; display: block;" width="878"/> </span> </p> <p style="text-align: center;"> <span style="font-size: 16px;"> Beast Querying Shadow Copies </span> </p> <p> <span style="font-size: 14px;"> <img alt="beast-ransomware-blog-14" height="117" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 846px) 100vw, 846px" src="https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-14.png?width=846&amp;height=117&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-14.png" srcset="https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-14.png?width=423&amp;height=59&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-14.png 423w, https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-14.png?width=846&amp;height=117&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-14.png 846w, https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-14.png?width=1269&amp;height=176&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-14.png 1269w, https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-14.png?width=1692&amp;height=234&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-14.png 1692w, https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-14.png?width=2115&amp;height=293&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-14.png 2115w, https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-14.png?width=2538&amp;height=351&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-14.png 2538w" style="height: auto; max-width: 100%; width: 846px;" width="846"/> </span> </p> <p style="text-align: center; font-size: 16px;"> Beast Deleting Shadow Copies </p> <h3 style="font-size: 30px; font-weight: normal;"> <span style="color: #000000;"> File Encryption </span> </h3> <p> Ransomware often employs multithreading to accelerate file encryption. </p> <p> This technique involves the parent thread identifying and sending files for encryption to child threads. </p> <p> The child threads then work concurrently, each encrypting a different file, significantly speeding up the overall encryption process. This approach leverages the system's hardware capabilities to encrypt files more efficiently. </p> <p style="text-align: center;"> <img alt="beast-ransomware-blog-15" height="638" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 365px) 100vw, 365px" src="https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-15.png?width=365&amp;height=638&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-15.png" srcset="https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-15.png?width=183&amp;height=319&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-15.png 183w, https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-15.png?width=365&amp;height=638&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-15.png 365w, https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-15.png?width=548&amp;height=957&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-15.png 548w, https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-15.png?width=730&amp;height=1276&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-15.png 730w, https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-15.png?width=913&amp;height=1595&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-15.png 913w, https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-15.png?width=1095&amp;height=1914&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-15.png 1095w" style="height: auto; max-width: 100%; width: 365px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; display: block;" width="365"/> </p> <p style="text-align: center; font-size: 16px;"> <em> Beast Ransomware Threads (demonstrating multithreading usage) </em> </p> <p> Beast uses powerful encryption methods to lock down files on all connected devices in a network. It targets a variety of file formats, such as documents, pictures, videos, and databases. </p> <p> Once files are encrypted, victims can't access them unless they have the decryption key, which is controlled by the attackers. </p> <p> <img alt="beast-ransomware-blog-16" height="179" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 887px) 100vw, 887px" src="https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-16.png?width=887&amp;height=179&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-16.png" srcset="https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-16.png?width=444&amp;height=90&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-16.png 444w, https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-16.png?width=887&amp;height=179&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-16.png 887w, https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-16.png?width=1331&amp;height=269&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-16.png 1331w, https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-16.png?width=1774&amp;height=358&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-16.png 1774w, https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-16.png?width=2218&amp;height=448&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-16.png 2218w, https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-16.png?width=2661&amp;height=537&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-16.png 2661w" style="height: auto; max-width: 100%; width: 887px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; display: block;" width="887"/> </p> <p style="text-align: center;"> <span style="font-size: 16px;"> <em> PDF File Encryption Process Example </em> </span> </p> <p> <img alt="beast-ransomware-blog-17" height="540" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 664px) 100vw, 664px" src="https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-17.png?width=664&amp;height=540&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-17.png" srcset="https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-17.png?width=332&amp;height=270&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-17.png 332w, https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-17.png?width=664&amp;height=540&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-17.png 664w, https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-17.png?width=996&amp;height=810&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-17.png 996w, https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-17.png?width=1328&amp;height=1080&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-17.png 1328w, https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-17.png?width=1660&amp;height=1350&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-17.png 1660w, https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-17.png?width=1992&amp;height=1620&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-17.png 1992w" style="height: auto; max-width: 100%; width: 664px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; display: block;" width="664"/> </p> <p style="text-align: center;"> <span style="font-size: 16px;"> <em> Encrypted Files </em> </span> </p> <p> The ransom note thread extracts and decodes the embedded ransom note, which was specified in the malware's settings. This note is then saved as a "README.txt" file in every directory that isn't explicitly excluded from encryption. </p> <p> <img alt="beast-ransomware-blog-18" height="51" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 878px) 100vw, 878px" src="https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-18.png?width=878&amp;height=51&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-18.png" srcset="https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-18.png?width=439&amp;height=26&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-18.png 439w, https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-18.png?width=878&amp;height=51&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-18.png 878w, https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-18.png?width=1317&amp;height=77&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-18.png 1317w, https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-18.png?width=1756&amp;height=102&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-18.png 1756w, https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-18.png?width=2195&amp;height=128&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-18.png 2195w, https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-18.png?width=2634&amp;height=153&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-18.png 2634w" style="height: auto; max-width: 100%; width: 878px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; display: block;" width="878"/> </p> <p style="text-align: center; font-size: 16px;"> <em> Creation Of The Ransom Note README.txt </em> </p> <p> <img alt="beast-ransomware-blog-19" height="404" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 904px) 100vw, 904px" src="https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-19.png?width=904&amp;height=404&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-19.png" srcset="https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-19.png?width=452&amp;height=202&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-19.png 452w, https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-19.png?width=904&amp;height=404&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-19.png 904w, https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-19.png?width=1356&amp;height=606&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-19.png 1356w, https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-19.png?width=1808&amp;height=808&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-19.png 1808w, https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-19.png?width=2260&amp;height=1010&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-19.png 2260w, https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-19.png?width=2712&amp;height=1212&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-19.png 2712w" style="height: auto; max-width: 100%; width: 904px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; display: block;" width="904"/> </p> <p style="text-align: center; font-size: 16px;"> <em> Ransom Note </em> </p> <p> In order to see Beast Ransomware GUI during the encryption process, it is needed to press and hold ALT+CTRL and type <strong> <em> 666 </em> </strong> : </p> <p> <img alt="beast-ransomware-blog-20" height="494" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 649px) 100vw, 649px" src="https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-20.png?width=649&amp;height=494&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-20.png" srcset="https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-20.png?width=325&amp;height=247&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-20.png 325w, https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-20.png?width=649&amp;height=494&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-20.png 649w, https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-20.png?width=974&amp;height=741&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-20.png 974w, https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-20.png?width=1298&amp;height=988&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-20.png 1298w, https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-20.png?width=1623&amp;height=1235&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-20.png 1623w, https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/blog-images/beast-ransomware-blog-20.png?width=1947&amp;height=1482&amp;name=beast-ransomware-blog-20.png 1947w" style="height: auto; max-width: 100%; width: 649px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; display: block;" width="649"/> </p> <p style="text-align: center; font-size: 16px;"> <em> Beast Ransomware GUI </em> </p> <h3 style="font-size: 30px; font-weight: normal;"> <span style="color: #000000;"> Indicators of Compromise - </span> <span style="color: #000000;"> IOCs </span> </h3> <p> Cybereason shared a list of indicators of compromise related to this research : </p> <table style="border-collapse: collapse; table-layout: fixed; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; border: 1px solid #99acc2;"> <tbody> <tr> <td style="background-color: #b7b7b7; border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p style="text-align: center;"> <span style="font-size: 14px;"> <strong> <span style="color: #ffffff;"> IOC </span> </strong> </span> </p> </td> <td style="background-color: #b7b7b7; border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p style="text-align: center;"> <span style="font-size: 14px;"> <strong> <span style="color: #ffffff;"> IOC type </span> </strong> </span> </p> </td> <td style="background-color: #b7b7b7; border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p style="text-align: center;"> <span style="font-size: 14px;"> <strong> <span style="color: #ffffff;"> Description </span> </strong> </span> </p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p> <span style="font-size: 14px;"> iplogger[.]co/1v1i85[.]torrent </span> </p> </td> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p style="text-align: center;"> <span style="font-size: 14px;"> Domain Name </span> </p> </td> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p style="text-align: center;"> <span style="font-size: 14px;"> Geofencing IP query </span> </p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p> <span style="font-size: 14px;"> 4c44ac1eea4bc7f4ea542d611b5658d7ac2729d79abe750da83f1581cd832eaf </span> </p> </td> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p style="text-align: center;"> <span style="font-size: 14px;"> SHA-256 </span> </p> </td> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p style="text-align: center;"> <span style="font-size: 14px;"> Beast Windows Encryptor </span> </p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p> <span style="background-color: #f9fafb; font-size: 14px;"> 369034bf1d793fe56ea4d683a156722d825ad9829fc128117f82a26bc1d0480b </span> </p> </td> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p style="text-align: center;"> <span style="font-size: 14px;"> SHA-256 </span> </p> </td> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p style="text-align: center;"> <span style="font-size: 14px;"> Beast Windows Encryptor </span> </p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p> <span style="background-color: #f9fafb; font-size: 14px;"> e01f5c7067dc984dceb883b10444b1a5b0f22ebd500baf9d9a88207f5033285d </span> </p> </td> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p style="text-align: center;"> <span style="font-size: 14px;"> SHA-256 </span> </p> </td> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p style="text-align: center;"> <span style="font-size: 14px;"> Beast Windows Encryptor </span> </p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p> <span style="background-color: #f9fafb; font-size: 14px;"> dd09a2ef31d018fd83f186e3eaaccccdaa8a8c8779ced668abb06dc934d89a2d </span> </p> </td> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p style="text-align: center;"> <span style="font-size: 14px;"> SHA-256 </span> </p> </td> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p style="text-align: center;"> <span style="font-size: 14px;"> Beast Windows Encryptor </span> </p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p> <span style="background-color: #f9fafb; font-size: 14px;"> dbbe792e6c804518909f8990a836552573522d126547429d6cd3fcb1f60d542c </span> </p> </td> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p style="text-align: center;"> <span style="font-size: 14px;"> SHA-256 </span> </p> </td> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p style="text-align: center;"> <span style="font-size: 14px;"> Beast Windows Encryptor </span> </p> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p style="text-align: left;"> </p> <h3 style="font-size: 30px; font-weight: normal;"> <span style="color: #000000;"> Cybereason Recommendations: </span> </h3> <ul> <li aria-level="1"> Follow and hunt Beast affiliate activity in order to identify pre-ransomware behaviors. </li> <li aria-level="1"> Promote cybersecurity best practices such as multifactor authentication and patch management. </li> <li aria-level="1"> For Cybereason customers on the Cybereason Defense Platform: <ul> <li aria-level="2"> Enable Anti-Malware and set the Anti-Malware &gt; Signatures mode to Prevent, Quarantine, or Disinfect. </li> <li aria-level="2"> Enable Anti-Ransomware (PRP), set Anti-Ransomware to Quarantine mode and enable shadow copy protection. </li> <li aria-level="2"> Enable Application Control. </li> <li aria-level="2"> Keep systems fully patched: Make sure your systems are patched in order to mitigate vulnerabilities. </li> <li aria-level="2"> Regularly backup files and create a backup process and policy : Restoring your files from a backup is the fastest way to regain access to your data. </li> <li aria-level="2"> Enable Variant Payload Prevention with prevent mode on Cybereason Behavioral execution prevention. <br/> <br/> </li> </ul> </li> </ul> <h3 style="font-size: 30px; font-weight: normal;"> <span style="color: #000000;"> MITRE ATT&amp;CK MAPPING </span> </h3> <table style="border-collapse: collapse; table-layout: fixed; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; border: 1px solid #99acc2;"> <thead> <tr> <th style="background-color: #b7b7b7; border-width: 1px; border-style: solid; vertical-align: middle;"> <p style="text-align: center;"> <span style="color: #ffffff;"> Tactic </span> </p> </th> <th style="background-color: #b7b7b7; border-width: 1px; border-style: solid; vertical-align: middle;"> <p style="text-align: center;"> <span style="color: #ffffff;"> Techniques / Sub-Techniques </span> </p> </th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p> TA0002: Execution </p> </td> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p> T1047 – Windows Management Instrumentation </p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p> TA0002: Execution </p> </td> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p> T1106 - Native API </p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p> TA0003: Persistence </p> </td> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p> T1543.003 – Create or Modify System Process: Windows Service </p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p> TA0007: Discovery </p> </td> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p> T1083 - File and Directory Discovery </p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p> TA0004: Privilege Escalation </p> </td> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p> T1078.001 – Valid Accounts: Default Accounts </p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p> TA0004: Privilege Escalation </p> </td> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p> T1078.002 – Valid Accounts: Domain Accounts </p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p> TA0007: Discovery </p> </td> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p> T1135 - Network Share Discovery </p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p> TA0007: Discovery </p> </td> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p> T1016 - System Network Configuration Discovery </p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p> TA0005: Defense Evasion </p> </td> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p> T1406.002 – Obfuscated Files or Information: Software Packing </p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p> TA0005: Defense Evasion </p> </td> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p> T1620 - Reflective Code Loading </p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p> TA0008: Lateral Movement </p> </td> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p> T1021.002 - Remote Service: SMB/Windows Admin Shares </p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p> TA0009: Collection </p> </td> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p> T1119 – Automated Collection </p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p> TA0040: Impact </p> </td> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p> T1486 - Data Encrypted for Impact </p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p> TA0040: Impact </p> </td> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p> T1489 – Service Stop </p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p> TA0040: Impact </p> </td> <td style="border: 1pt solid #000000;"> <p> T1490 – Inhibit System Recovery </p> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p> </p> <h3 style="font-size: 30px; font-weight: normal;"> <span style="color: #434343;"> References </span> </h3> <p> <a href="https://blogs.blackberry.com/en/2022/09/some-kind-of-monster-raas-hides-itself-using-traits-from-other-malware"> <span> https://blogs.blackberry.com/en/2022/09/some-kind-of-monster-raas-hides-itself-using-traits-from-other-malware </span> </a> </p> <p> <a href="https://cyberint.com/blog/research/the-nature-of-the-beast-ransomware/"> <span> https://cyberint.com/blog/research/the-nature-of-the-beast-ransomware/ </span> </a> </p> <p> </p> <h3 style="font-size: 30px; font-weight: normal;"> <span style="color: #000000;"> ABOUT THE RESEARCHER </span> </h3> <p> <strong> Mark Tsipershtein, Security Researcher at Cybereason </strong> <img alt="mark-tsipershtein-hs" height="149" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 152px) 100vw, 152px" src="https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/headshots/mark-tsipershtein-hs.png?width=152&amp;height=149&amp;name=mark-tsipershtein-hs.png" srcset="https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/headshots/mark-tsipershtein-hs.png?width=76&amp;height=75&amp;name=mark-tsipershtein-hs.png 76w, https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/headshots/mark-tsipershtein-hs.png?width=152&amp;height=149&amp;name=mark-tsipershtein-hs.png 152w, https://www.cybereason.com/hs-fs/hubfs/dam/images/images-web/