[31mCrawled page content: [0m ['Fletch - Beast Ransomware: RaaS Platform Targets Windows, Linux, and VMware ESXi - #Beast>\nBeast Ransomware: RaaS Platform Targets Windows, Linux, and VMware ESXi - #Beast\nThe Beast Ransomware, also known as Monster, is a Ransomware-as-a-Service (RaaS) platform that has been targeting Windows, Linux, and ESXi systems since 2022. This malware allows affiliates to customize ransomware binaries and includes advanced encryption methods like Elliptic-curve cryptography and ChaCha20. It avoids Commonwealth of Independent States (CIS) countries, likely to evade local law enforcement. The ransomware spreads through SMB scans and exploits system components like the Restart Manager for efficient execution, also deleting shadow copies to prevent file recovery. Cybereason emphasizes the importance of cybersecurity practices like multifactor authentication, patch management, and regular backups for detection and prevention against Beast ransomware.']
