y Awareness Training Emails\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0*\nMrbMiner Malware\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0*\nMFA Bypass Vulnerability in Microsoft 365\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0*\nPrometei Multi-Modular Botnet\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0*\nEmotet Malware New Spamming Campaign\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0*\nLemon Duck Cryptominer\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0*\nQakbot malware\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0*\nTrojan Glupteba\nBeast Ransomware RaaS Service Platform Targets Windows, Linux, and VMware ESXi\nPublish Date: 2024-10-21\nDescription\nA recent analysis by Cybereason highlights the evolving landscape of Beast Ransomware, a Ransomware-as-a-Service (RaaS) platform that has been actively targeting organizations since 2022. Known also as Monster, this malware has gained traction among cybercriminals for its adaptable features, allowing affiliates to customize attacks across various operating systems, including Windows, Linux, and VMware ESXi servers.\n\nBeast stands out for its extensive tools and regular updates that appeal to a wide range of users within the cybercrime community. Attackers can design specialized payloads aimed at maximizing damage. For Windows, the ransomware employs advanced encryption techniques such as Elliptic-curve cryptography paired with ChaCha20, utilizing a multithreaded process for efficient file encryption while shutting down essential services to minimize data disruption.\n\nThe platform’s cross-operational capability is significant. The Windows variant can package files into ZIP archives containing ransom notes, while the Linux and ESXi versions are designed to halt virtual machines before executing encryption. A recent update introduced an offline builder, enabling the creation of ransomware specifically for Windows, NAS, and ESXi systems without needing an internet connection, thus increasing its adaptability.\n\nA particularly concerning aspect of Beast is its ability to self-propagate via SMB scans, which allows it to swiftly infect vulnerable systems within the same network. Interestingly, it avoids encrypting devices in Commonwealth of Independent States (CIS) countries, likely to evade local law enforcement. To obstruct recovery attempts, Beast also targets Windows shadow copies, eliminating backups to ensure victims cannot restore their files.\nShare\nAffected Platform(s) / Version(s)\nWindows, Linux, VMware ESXi\nDistribution Method\nUnauthorised Access\nAttack Type\nRansomware Attack\nAttack Source\nBeast Ransomware\nRegion\nGlobal\nAffected Business(s)\nMultiple Sectors\nRecommendations\nSecurity administrators should block the IoCs on all applicable security solutions post-validation.\nSecurity administrators should ensure that all applications, databases, servers, and network devices are periodically hardened and adequately configured.\nEnsure regular backups of critical data and store them offline or in a secure cloud environment to avoid ransomware encryption.\nUsers should not download suspicious applications or attachments received over the internet and be alert to social engineering and phishing attacks.\nUsers should not download, accept, or execute files and do not visit websites or follow links provided by unknown or untrusted sources.\nSecurity administrators should regularly take Backup of the applications, databases, and all critical data.\nSecurity administrators should apply the Principle of Least Privilege to all systems and services.\nKeep AV signatures, operating systems, and third-party applications up to date on all systems, mobile devices, and servers.\nReferences\nhttps://www.cybereason.com/blog/threat-analysis-beast-ransomware\nhttps://securityonline.info/beast-ransomware-raas-platform-targets-windows-linux-and-vmware-esxi/#google_vignette\nIOC FILE:\nIoCs_Beast_Ransomware_21_10_2024.xlsx\nProtect your Data and Brand Value from Data Breaches!\nInfoshare-Varutra provide security services 