# Enriched Doc (enrihcments marked with *content*(link)): 
 Incident: Beast Ransomware 

 Root cause: Initial compromises typically occur through phishing emails or compromised remote desktop protocol (RDP) endpoints. 

 Threat Actor/group/campaign: Beast Ransomware group (originating from Monster Ransomware), *operates as a RaaS Service Platform* (https://varutra.com/ctp/threatpost/postDetails/Beast-Ransomware-RaaS-Service-Platform-Targets-Windows,-Linux,-and-VMware-ESXi/M1hpM0prdlk3TnBKSFJDWW9yYjZLQT09). 

 Organization/industry/location: Various industries, no specific organization or location mentioned. 

 Start date – End date: Active since 2022, with recent updates promoted in June 2024. 

 MITRE TTPs: ['Execution: T1047 – Windows Management Instrumentation, T1106 - Native API', 'Persistence: T1543.003 – Create or Modify System Process: Windows Service', 'Discovery: T1083 - File and Directory Discovery, T1135 - Network Share Discovery, T1016 - System Network Configuration Discovery', 'Privilege Escalation: T1078.001 – Valid Accounts: Default Accounts, T1078.002 – Valid Accounts: Domain Accounts', 'Defense Evasion: T1406.002 – Obfuscated Files or Information: Software Packing, T1620 - Reflective Code Loading', 'Lateral Movement: T1021.002 - Remote Service: SMB/Windows Admin Shares', 'Collection: T1119 – Automated Collection', 'Impact: T1486 - Data Encrypted for Impact, T1489 – Service Stop, T1490 – Inhibit System Recovery'] 

 Impact: Data encryption across Windows, Linux, and ESXi systems, significant data loss and operational disruption for affected organizations. *Enhanced speed and new command line options for encryption* (https://cyberint.com/blog/research/the-nature-of-the-beast-ransomware/), *advanced encryption methods like Elliptic-curve cryptography and ChaCha20* (https://cs.beta.fletch.ai/p/beast). 

