  "final_report": {
    "Incident": "GHOSTPULSE’s new pixel-level deception",
    "Root cause": "The root cause behind the incident is the use of advanced techniques by the GHOSTPULSE malware to embed its malicious payload within the pixel structures of image files. This evolution makes detection more challenging and exploits social engineering tactics to execute malicious commands. *The campaign leverages signed MSIX application packages for initial access via a stealthy loader* (https://github.com/elastic/labs-releases/tree/main/tools/ghostpulse).",
    "Threat Actor/group/campaign": "GHOSTPULSE malware family, also known as HIJACKLOADER or IDATLOADER, with possible utilization by LUMMA STEALER for recent campaigns.",
    "Organization/industry/location": "Not specifically targeted at a single organization or industry; the malware is used in diverse campaigns.",
    "Start date – End date": "The updated version of GHOSTPULSE was observed starting from October 2024.",
    "MITRE TTPs": "T1055.012 Process Injection: XOR decryption technique and Windows API utilization; T1036.003 Masquerading: Embedding malicious payloads within pixel structures of images; T1566.001 Phishing: Creative social engineering tactics involving CAPTCHA validations.",
    "Impact": "Multiple individuals and organizations impacted due to the deceptive techniques that bypass traditional detection methods.",
    "Mitigation": "- Implement robust email and web filtering solutions to block malicious attachments and links.\n- Educate employees about the risks of social engineering tactics, such as fake CAPTCHA validations.\n- Deploy advanced endpoint detection and response (EDR) tools that can detect unusual activity and behavior-based anomalies.\n- Regularly update and patch software to avoid exploitation of known vulnerabilities.\n- Utilize updated YARA rules and configuration extractors to detect and analyze GHOSTPULSE malware.\n- *Use the GHOSTPULSE payload extractor to analyze encrypted files* (https://github.com/elastic/labs-releases/tree/main/tools/ghostpulse).",
    "Detailed Steps for mitigation": "1. Block suspicious domains and IPs associated with GHOSTPULSE and LUMMA STEALER campaigns.\n2. Regularly review and update security policies to include detection and response for pixel-based malware techniques.\n3. Conduct regular training sessions for employees on identifying phishing attempts and social engineering tactics.\n4. Integrate threat intelligence feeds into security systems to stay updated on emerging threats.\n5. *Ensure Python 3.10 environment for running the GHOSTPULSE payload extractor* (https://github.com/elastic/labs-releases/tree/main/tools/ghostpulse).",
